BND-01: give a FREE/NORMAL outfall below a regulator no offset depth

Since 5.3.0, outfall_setOutletDepth() sets a FREE outfall to z + MIN(yNorm,
yCrit) and a NORMAL one to z + yNorm, where z is the link's downstream
offset. For a conduit that is the height of the pipe invert above the
outfall. For a weir, orifice or outlet, link_setParams() copies the crest
offset into offset2, so z is the crest height above the UPSTREAM node and
the outfall gets that as a fake tailwater depth. Use z = 0 for a non-conduit
link whose downstream node is the outfall, which restores the 5.2.4 result
(depth 0) for regulators and leaves conduits unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-01_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/link.c b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
index 31925e1..ac2b624 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/link.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
@@ -747,6 +747,10 @@ void link_setOutfallDepth(int j)
     {
         n = Link[j].node2;
         z = Link[j].offset2;
+
+        // --- a regulator's offset2 is its crest height above its upstream
+        //     node, not a height above the outfall
+        if ( Link[j].type != CONDUIT ) z = 0.0;
     }
     else if ( Node[Link[j].node1].type == OUTFALL )
     {
